{# Repair - Cryosurgical Handpiece (Figma 35098:39248, the client's 1600px frame on the WIP page); the URL is the
   live site's. No redesigned or phone frame exists, so the sections use the redesign's components and type scale, as
   on Micro Instrument Repair:
   - Hero: the shared content hero with the frame's photo and fade, the title and the frame's intro (drawn under the
     hero in Figma). Figma's hero button "Download Repair Form" is left out, as on Micro Instrument Repair: the form
     is downloaded from the request strip under the prices, which the intro points to.
   - "Typical Repair Charges": the frame's three level cards with the micro price tables' look (navy header, 1px
     #dde7ee border, 4px corners). Under them the warranty line, not in orange text (too light on white) but with
     an orange shield, and the first disclaimer, which says what the prices are for.
   - "Request a Repair": the shared strip, with the hero photo.
   - No Free Lifetime Repair band: cryosurgical handpieces are excluded from the programme.
   - "SEO Text": the PLP features list (bold lead-in, orange dashes).
   - "Disclaimers": the other three lines as fine print, where the frame has them.
   - FAQ: the shared FAQ section; it loads closed (Figma's orange question is a hover example) and the answers
     are the live page's. #}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{% import "content/macros.njk" as c with context %}
{% import "plp/macros.njk" as plp_ui with context %}
{% set cr = contentPages.cryo %}

{{ ui.breadcrumbs([{ label: "Repair Services", href: "/repair-services/" }, { label: "Cryosurgical Handpiece" }]) }}

{# Hero: the handpieces photo (blue all over) under the frame's fade (cryoFade). From xl the photo is Figma's
   1849x693 (the screen's width from 1849px, so it always reaches the right edge), with the probe tip (43.7% across
   the photo) 60px past the 593px text column: never left of 123px before the screen's edge, which puts the tip at
   685px up to 1600px. From lg to xl it is 1450px wide with the tip at 685px, so more of the handpieces fits beside
   the text. The photo is centred on the hero's height a little high (54%), which keeps both handpieces in view on
   wide screens (Figma's 107px above the hero at 1600). Phones and tablets have no room beside the text: the photo
   covers the hero with the handpieces on the right, under the phone fade (also on tablets, where cryoFade would
   cover all of it) and a 60% navy tint that keeps the white text readable over the light blue. #}
{{ c.hero({
  title: "Cryosurgical Handpiece Repair", text: cr.intro, figma: "35098:39315", image: "077f3d82",
  fade: contentPages.gradients.cryoFade, fadeAt: "lg",
  photo: "inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-[80%_70%] lg:inset-auto lg:left-[51px] lg:top-1/2 lg:h-auto lg:w-[1450px] lg:max-w-none lg:-translate-y-[54%] xl:left-[max(-123px,calc(50%_-_115px_-_max(808px,43.7%)))] xl:w-[max(1849px,100%)]",
  scrim: "bg-primary-500/60 lg:hidden"
}) }}

{# Typical Repair Charges ("Charges" 35098:39328, the intro moved into the hero): 36px between the title and the
   cards, as above the micro price tables. Cards: navy header with the level and its price range (Bold 24/32 white,
   centred as drawn; phones 20/28), Regular 18/28 navy text with Figma's 32px sides (phones 16/24, 20px), three in a
   row from xl, stacked below. The notes and the request strip follow with the cards' gap. #}
<section class="bg-white" aria-labelledby="charges-title" data-figma="35098:39328">
  <div class="container-page flex flex-col gap-6 py-10 md:gap-9 md:py-[50px]">
    <h2 id="charges-title" class="text-h3 font-medium text-heading md:text-h2 md:font-bold lg:text-h1" data-figma="35098:39329">Typical Repair Charges</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 md:gap-6">
      <ul class="grid gap-4 md:gap-6 xl:grid-cols-3" data-figma="35098:39330">
        {% for lv in cr.levels %}
        <li class="flex min-w-0 flex-col" data-figma="{{ lv.figma }}">
          <h3 class="rounded-t bg-primary-500 px-4 py-3 text-center text-h4 font-bold text-white md:py-4 md:text-h3">{{ lv.name }}: {{ lv.price }}</h3>
          <p class="flex-1 rounded-b border border-t-0 border-outline px-5 py-6 text-base text-primary-500 md:px-8 md:text-lg">{{ lv.text }}</p>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2" data-figma="35098:39346">
        <p class="flex items-start gap-3 text-base font-bold text-heading md:text-lg">{% icon "shield-check", "h-6 w-6 shrink-0 text-accent md:mt-0.5" %}<span>{{ cr.warranty }}</span></p>
        <p class="text-sm text-body md:text-base">{{ cr.pricingNote }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {# The hero photo cropped to the handpieces, fading in from the strip's tint: from md the right 55% of the strip,
       the handpieces under the button; phones: a 120px band along the bottom, under the full-width button. #}
    {{ c.requestStrip({
      image: "077f3d82",
      photo: "inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-[120px] w-full object-cover object-[85%_75%] [mask-image:linear-gradient(180deg,transparent,#000_60%)] md:inset-x-auto md:inset-y-0 md:right-0 md:h-full md:w-[55%] md:object-[100%_60%] md:[mask-image:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent,#000_45%)]"
    }) }}
  </div>
</section>

<div class="pb-8 md:pb-10">{{ plp_ui.features(cr.seo) }}</div>

{# Disclaimers (35098:39350): fine print after the features, with the Free Lifetime Repair fine print's line above
   it; centred from md as drawn. #}
<section class="border-t border-outline bg-white" aria-label="Disclaimers" data-figma="35098:39350">
  <div class="container-page flex flex-col gap-1 py-6 text-sm text-body md:py-8 md:text-center">
    {% for d in cr.disclaimers %}<p>{{ d }}</p>{% endfor %}
  </div>
</section>

